---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  locale="en"
  page="terms"
  title="Terms of Use — SimTether"
  description="SimTether terms of use — what the purchase covers, the hosted relay, and acceptable use."
>
  <section class="prose">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Terms of Use</h2>
      <p><strong>Effective date:</strong> September 27, 2026<br />
         <strong>Contact:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/wissam53/simtether/issues">github.com/wissam53/simtether</a></p>

      <h3>What you're buying</h3>
      <p>The SimTether client app is a <strong>one-time purchase</strong> through
         Google Play that unlocks the app permanently — no subscription and
         no expiry. The bridge app is free and open source.</p>
      <p>Refunds follow <strong>Google Play's refund policy</strong> — we don't
         process payments ourselves and can't issue refunds directly; Play
         handles them. Given how Android background limits and power management
         vary across manufacturers and devices, we recommend testing pairing,
         SMS delivery, calls, and service persistence on your phones within
         Google Play's refund window.</p>

      <h3>The hosted relay</h3>
      <p>Remote access through our hosted relay is a <strong>best-effort
         service provided at no charge</strong>. We may change, suspend, or
         discontinue it at any time, and we may introduce a charge for hosted
         relay access in the future. The app purchase does not include any
         commitment that hosted relay access remains free or available.</p>
      <p>What is guaranteed: <strong>local and hotspot modes require no
         paid service</strong>, and you can always run your own relay using
         the open-source software. The app never depends on our
         infrastructure to function. If the hosted relay stops or becomes
         paid, nothing else about the app changes.</p>

      <h3>Use it on your own devices</h3>
      <p>SimTether is for forwarding <strong>your own SIM's</strong> SMS and
         calls between <strong>phones you own or control</strong>. You must
         not use it to monitor, intercept, or forward another person's
         messages or calls without their knowledge. The bridge phone displays
         a persistent notification whenever the service is active — that
         visibility is intentional and must not be disabled to conceal the
         service from the phone's owner. Interception of communications you
         are not a party to is illegal in most jurisdictions.</p>
      <p>SimTether forwards data — it does not modify, spoof, or circumvent
         device or network registration requirements. The SIM must remain in a
         legally registered device. You are responsible for complying with the
         telecommunications regulations that apply in your country.</p>

      <h3>Disclaimer and warranties</h3>
      <p>The apps are provided "as is". They relay your own carrier traffic;
         SMS delivery, call behaviour, and USSD/service-code support depend
         on your carrier, SIM, and phone manufacturer — we can't guarantee
         carrier behaviour. Battery-management systems on some phones (Xiaomi,
         Oppo, others) can kill background services; the app shows health
         warnings for this but the device's owner is responsible for the
         manufacturer's settings. To the extent permitted by law, we are not
         liable for missed messages, missed calls, or carrier charges.</p>

      <h3>Changes</h3>
      <p>If these terms change, the effective date above moves and the changes
         are recorded in the public repository history.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
